  "behavior": [
    "The existing server remains the sole session/grant authority. Canonical response validators reject unknown fields, invalid timestamps, impossible lifetimes and inconsistent inventories.",
    "Private P-256 keys are nonextractable. Session-only keys remain in mounted request-controller memory; an explicitly approved remembered key is saved only in origin-scoped IndexedDB, after protected access is verified.",
    "The notice opens explicit approval. Both browsers compare a code; remember intent defaults off and requires both decisions. Settings displays session-only and remembered expiry/last use and supports revocation and local forgetting as distinct actions.",
    "Storage success means transaction completion. Abort, blocked/quota failure and deadlines do not earn saved status or trigger raw-key fallback. Forget confirmation also waits for committed deletion.",
    "Fresh protected inspection confirms proof usability. A lost response may recover an already active session after the request deadline without another proof or grant. Remembered persistence remains unconfirmed when metadata was lost.",
    "Confirmation and optional restoration share the existing 15-second signal. Late module, lock, load, signing and proof outcomes cannot publish a cancelled restore or initiate another proof. Session-check notifications trigger protected inventory inspection and cannot grant authentication.",
    "Requester echo, key identity, remembered intent, origin, installation and renewal grant bindings remain explicit. Invalid response binding emits body-free diagnostics. Browser wall-clock precision does not override server challenge expiry or single use.",
    "All stage evidence uses the existing client diagnostic transport and registered Activity Log formatter with closed operation/outcome fields. No key material, signatures, comparison codes or approval identifiers enter those diagnostics."
  ],
