    "scope": "Actual product key-store/crypto/evidence modules bundled with production NODE_ENV. Isolated persistent browser profiles are closed/reopened, signatures are independently checked with the public key, and an actual transaction aborts after put success. This is not a protected approval/draft/SSD journey.",
    "environmentFailures": "Initial fixture bundling omitted production NODE_ENV, and Firefox initially failed profile lookup. Earlier failures remain retained. Linux Firefox uses a private writable existing home path, 512 MiB shared memory and 256 PID limit; no HOME override, host profile or sandbox disablement.",
    "linuxImage": "mcr.microsoft.com/playwright@sha256:a0f4498920a5dbac63196d9140ed738ef00470f27e2e74029abd8850b7bd5717",
    "containerConstraints": "Offline, UID 1000, all capabilities dropped, no-new-privileges, read-only product source/root filesystem, private tmpfs/home/profile, repository test seccomp profile, bounded CPU/memory/PIDs.",
    "telemetryCorrection": "The original private harness inspected meta.browserApproval instead of meta.stageReport.browserApproval, so its no-stored-claim assertion was vacuous. Original harnesses/receipts remain retained. These fresh runs require a genuine successful-commit positive control before testing the actual aborted-put negative; no historical telemetry credit is reassigned.",
