  "failureFirst": {
    "lateProofResponse": "Two failed and three healthy client controls before reconciliation; the same five then pass within the 143-test owning run. Six extended independent actual-route/registry/crypto controls pass, preserving grant/session identity and expiry.",
    "requesterIntent": "One failed and twelve healthy service controls before checking the human remember echo; all thirteen pass afterward.",
    "routeVocabulary": "The two exact production route-vocabulary controls fail with eight healthy controls before adding challenge/prove/request; all ten pass afterward. Unknown/private segments remain elided.",
    "integration": "Initial full UI run: six failures, 10735 passes and one existing skip. Pair/navigation/replay transport seams, styling prefix and actual browser boot/deadline integration repaired; initial targeted nine suites pass 117 tests. Full follow-up before added storage unit controls passes 10747 tests with the same existing skip.",
    "groundingFixture": "The logging increment exposes eleven failures in the existing grounding suite: a newly mounted independent Notice produces its own legitimate diagnostic. The child boundary is isolated without changing any exact grounding assertions. Five dedicated Notice lifecycle tests verify self-revoke, acknowledged/failed repair, focus and stale cancelled-response handling."
  },
